# To the Stone Mouth — the Howe's walk, its last stretch to the gate: D minor, a slow tread on a
# muffled drum, the shadows' motif low in a trombone, voices rising toward the mouth. Original,
# cb17 (2026-10-29). 4 bars of 4/4 at 60: 16 s, a loop.
